WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.592
A parameter is a placeholder name inside the function definition.

00:00:04.592 --> 00:00:09.492
An argument is the actual value supplied when the function is called.

00:00:09.492 --> 00:00:13.822
In def greet name, name is the parameter.

00:00:13.822 --> 00:00:18.103
When we call greet with Avery, Avery is the argument.

00:00:18.593 --> 00:00:22.040
Think of the parameter as an empty labeled slot.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.645
The argument is the value we place into that slot for one particular function call.
